   "title": "HOW TO USE",
   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote",
    "ue_properties": {
     "widget_ue_connectable": {},
     "version": "7.8",
     "input_ue_unconnectable": {}
    }
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "# Ultimate LTX — how to use\n\nWork top to bottom: **Setup → Models → Output → Director → Seeds → Finish**. Everything is chosen up front; after a seed hunt only **WINNER** is left.\n\n## 1 · SETUP — how the seeds are rendered\n- **seeds** — how many full videos (with sound) to render, 1–4.\n- **seed** — seed 1; seeds 2–4 add 1000003 each. Keep its **control after generate on fixed**, or the finish re-renders new seeds.\n- **steps / sampler / scheduler / cfg** — 8 steps, euler_ancestral, linear_quadratic, cfg 1: the official distilled first pass (linear_quadratic at 8 steps is exactly Lightricks' distilled sigmas).\n- **first pass scale** — the seeds render at this fraction of the Director's size; Finish's latent upscaler takes the winner back up (x2 upscaler → 0.5).\n- Changing anything here **re-renders** the seeds.\n\n## 2 · MODELS — what it runs on\n- **diffusion model** — the LTX 2.5 checkpoint (safetensors or GGUF). A non-distilled checkpoint needs the **distill LoRA** (8 steps, cfg 1); the Stubelius remix has it baked in.\n- **extra LoRA 1–2** — apply to the seeds and the refine. **IC-LoRA** — for the Director's motion / video guides.\n- **text encoder, video / audio VAE, latent upscaler** — LTX 2.5 files (2.5 needs the Gemma 4 encoder).\n- **speed & memory** — Sage attention; memory-efficient attention and chunked feed-forward use less VRAM. **decode tile size** — each clip is decoded in one temporal pass (no flicker between chunks); lower the tile if the decode runs out of VRAM.\n- **live preview** — tiny LTX VAE for the **LIVE PREVIEW** panel; off = ComfyUI's default preview on the sampling node.\n\n## 3 · OUTPUT — what comes out (set it now, change it any time)\n- **refine strength / steps / sampler** — the winner is upscaled x2 in latent space and refined at full size from this noise level. 0.3–0.45 keeps the seed's look and adds detail; the official two-stage template restarts at 0.85–0.91, which re-imagines the detail and can change the whole look. euler = no new noise in the refine, as Lightricks' pipeline.\n- **audio** — keep the seed's sound exactly as you heard it, or let the refine regenerate it.\n- **final resolution** — native (the Director's size) or 720p–4K; the short side lands exactly on the number, portrait too. 4K holds ≈100 MB of RAM per frame: keep 4K clips short, especially at 48–60 fps.\n- **final fps** — 0 = the Director's frame rate, untouched; 48 / 50 / 60 via RIFE, length and sync kept, hard cuts stay clean.\n- **upscaler** — RTX VSR, or DLSS5 + Color Lock (more detail, original colours).\n- Output feeds only Finish, so changing it **never re-renders** the seeds.\n\n## 4 · DIRECTOR — what the video is\nThe timeline: prompts, images (first frame, last frame, keyframes), audio and motion tracks, size, frame rate and duration.\n\n## 5 · SEEDS and FINISH — pick the winner\n**winner** — which seed to finish; **0 = hold** after the seeds. That's the only choice left after a seed hunt.\n\n**Seed hunt:** set seeds = 3 and **winner = 0** (hold) and queue → watch Seed 1–3 → set winner 1–3 on Finish → queue again (only the finish runs; the seeds come from cache). Winner 1+ on the first run finishes that seed straight away. Don't touch Setup / Models / Director in between.\n"
   ],
   "color": "#241e2a",
   "bgcolor": "#1b1720"
